  "by_construction": {
    "holds_by_construction": [
      "Deterministic recall and precision on the keyed labelled items (2500 of 2500 faults, 0 of 2500 near-misses flagged): each keyed subtype restates its lint's trigger, and card L2's label check fails the set unless every keyed fault is flagged and no near-miss is. They are a regression check on card L1's lints, not evidence for H3's statement that deterministic lints find seeded faults with useful precision.",
      "Deterministic recall on the unkeyed items (0 of 2000 faults): no deterministic lint is built for what makes an unkeyed item faulty, which is in its text only.",
      "Recall on wrong-scope, 0 under either tier: its labels name no lint, and a finding by a lint a label does not name gives it no credit.",
      "Per keyed lint, recall and precision on its own labels (500 of 500 faults found, no near-miss flagged, for each of the five): the same restated triggers."
    ],
    "measured": [
      "The findings on LongMemEval's own items (`unverified.base`): how many there are is measured; whether each is real is not known until members judge card L2's audit sample, so each lint's precision on natural memory is bounded only by 0 and 1 (`natural_memory`)."
    ],
    "not_natural_precision": "`precision_with_unverified` pools the labelled true positives, whose number the generator's injection rate fixes, with the unverified findings; its lower end moves with `per_question` and says nothing about precision on natural memory."
  },
